WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.736
In the Southern Dynasties there was a writer named Jiang Yan, who wrote exceptionally well when he was young.

00:00:06.086 --> 00:00:09.902
He came from a poor family, yet he studied and wrote with great diligence.

00:00:10.252 --> 00:00:14.284
Everyone praised his talent, and his works circulated everywhere.

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:19.458
Many famous people loved reading his writings and praised them endlessly.

00:00:19.808 --> 00:00:23.144
But one night, he had a strange dream.

00:00:23.494 --> 00:00:28.366
The scenes in the dream were so wondrous that he could not forget them for a long time.

00:00:28.716 --> 00:00:34.236
In the dream, a man asked him to give back a five-color brush, and he had no choice but to return it.

00:00:34.586 --> 00:00:40.634
That brush shone with five-colored light — it was the very source of his literary inspiration.

00:00:40.984 --> 00:00:46.288
From then on, his literary inspiration was never as good as before.

00:00:46.638 --> 00:00:51.630
He would pick up his brush wanting to write, yet for half a day could not write a thing.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:57.980
People then used 'Jiang Lang's talent is exhausted' to describe talent in decline — what a pity.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:03.010
This expression reminds us that talent, too, needs constant honing.

